# Keep every text file LF in the working tree, on every OS.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true produces CRLF files
# and two things break that look like real failures but are not:
#   * Vite's SSR transform does not recognise a `#!...\r\n` shebang, so it
#     hoists imports above it and the `#!` lands mid-line -> "SyntaxError:
#     Invalid or unexpected token" when a test imports scripts/*.mjs.
#   * Source-inspection tests match multi-line regexes against source files;
#     an unexpected \r before every \n makes those patterns miss.
# Both are invisible on Linux CI, so pin the line endings instead of teaching
# every test to tolerate \r.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary
*.node binary

# Windows-only files that genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
